/-!
# Power series presentations of complete local rings

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Theorem 032A, part (2) and its proof
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-cohen-structure-power-series-surjection).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace IsLocalRing

/-- A complete local ring with finitely generated maximal ideal is a quotient of a power series
ring over a characteristic-zero field or a Cohen ring of the residue characteristic.
Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Theorem 032A, part (2) and the final paragraph of its proof
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-cohen-structure-power-series-surjection).

Proof:
1. Choose finitely many generators `yᵢ` of the maximal ideal. Its powers are generated by the
   monomials of the corresponding total degree; completeness implies their intersection is zero
   (def-weil-pbc-adically-complete-ring).
2. If the residue characteristic is zero, choose the coefficient ring supplied by
   lem-weil-pbc-cohen-coefficient-ring-exists. Its maximal ideal is zero, and its residue map is
   an isomorphism to the residue field of `R`, so it is a characteristic-zero field.
3. In positive characteristic choose a Cohen ring with that residue field using
   lem-weil-pbc-cohen-rings-exist. Inductively lift its maps modulo powers of `p` to the quotients
   of `R` modulo powers of the maximal ideal: the successive kernels are square-zero, and
   lem-weil-pbc-cohen-ring-mod-pn-formally-smooth supplies each compatible lift.
4. Take the inverse limit of these maps (def-weil-pbc-adic-completion) and use the completeness
   of `R` (def-weil-pbc-adically-complete-ring) to obtain a coefficient map into `R` whose
   residue map is surjective.
5. Apply lem-weil-pbc-power-series-universal-property-complete to this coefficient map and the
   generators `yᵢ`, obtaining a map from MvPowerSeries (def-weil-pbc-multivariate-power-series).
6. Let `A` be that power series ring and `I` its variables ideal. It is complete by
   lem-weil-pbc-power-series-variables-complete. On the `A`-module `R` the submodules `I^k R`
   are exactly the powers of the maximal ideal, hence have zero intersection. The residue map
   from the coefficient ring is onto, so `1` generates `R/IR`. Applying
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-over-complete-ring shows that `1` generates `R` over `A`, which means
   the power series map is surjective. -/
theorem cohen_structure_power_series_surjection
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    (hfg : (maximalIdeal R).FG) [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R]
    (p : ℕ) [CharP (ResidueField R) p] :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (Λ : Type u) (_ : CommRing Λ),
      (p = 0 → IsField Λ ∧ CharZero Λ) ∧
      (0 < p → IsCohenRing p Λ) ∧
      ∃ φ : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →+* R, Function.Surjective φ := by
  sorry

end IsLocalRing
